      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Manokin Historic District preserves a cluster of 18th‑ and 19th‑century homes that tell the story of early Maryland settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manokin%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "As early as 1620, the Manonoakin people traded goods at Trading Point, the fork of Manokin River and Trading Branch, with English colonists.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.roads.maryland.gov/mdotsha/pages/pressreleasedetails.aspx?newsId=4870&PageId=818",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "On November 17, 2023, a new roadside historical marker was unveiled at the Somerset County Visitor Center to honor the Manonoakin Indian Town Site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
